WEBVTT

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:04.380
When should you start planning a
commercial lease renewal?

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.720
Start with your actual lease dates, not a
generic countdown.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.440
Ask your solicitor to confirm any option
window, the notice requirements and

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.400
who needs to receive it.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.960
Then set an earlier internal decision
date.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:20.060
Prepare a simple decision pack: your
verified dates, what the workplace needs

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:24.340
to do, the renewal proposal, realistic
alternatives, and the cash and delivery

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:25.540
implications of each option.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.880
Compare the same period and cost
categories.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.440
A lower starting rent alone does not tell
you whether moving is the better

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.260
business choice. And give every action an
owner.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.160
A reminder is useful, but it does not
issue notice or extend a deadline.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.120
Our Newcastle renewal guide includes a
free worksheet to organise the

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:46.240
comparison. If you need help with the
commercial brief and negotiations, start

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:49.040
a conversation with YOS alongside your
legal adviser.
